title: Getting started

! Getting started

# Install [[NetLogo 7.0.4|https://ccl.northwestern.edu/netlogo/download.shtml]].
# Download the zip for the version you want from its page: [[Baseline]], [[Soil]], [[Crowding]] or [[Combined]]. The zip contains the model file and a `data` folder.
# Unzip it and keep the `data` folder next to the model file. The model reads its map, settlement, water and climate files from `data`.
# Open the `.nlogox` file in NetLogo, press SETUP, then GO. The run stops after 1350.
# To repeat a run exactly, set `run-seed` before SETUP.

!! Reading the interface

* The population plot compares simulated households with the archaeological series.
* The "available sites vs carrying capacity" plot shows farm sites currently available next to `potential`.
* `map-view` switches between zones, water sources, yield and occupancy. Soil and Combined add a soil quality view.
* `historic-view?` shows the archaeological settlements as houses sized by the number of households.

!! BehaviorSpace

Each model except [[Crowding]] includes experiments under Tools > BehaviorSpace. The experiment names are listed on the model pages. The experiments' constants cover the model parameters, so check the interface values (including the [[Combined]] switches) before running them.

!! Code markers

Comments in the code mark which parts belong to which version:

|!Marker |!Meaning |
|`[BASELINE FIX]` |corrects behavior of the published model |
|`[BASELINE]` |seed control, measurement and reporting added to the published model |
|`[SOIL]` |dynamic soil quality |
|`[CROWDING]` |scarcity-driven plot sharing |
